  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/D1AD76">Definition <span data-tag="D1AD76">6.3.1.1</span>.</a>geometric morphism Let $\calX $ and $\calY $ be $\infty $-topoi. A <em>geometric morphism</em> from $\calX $ to $\calY $ is a functor $f_{\ast }: \calX \rightarrow \calY $ which admits a left exact left adjoint (which we will typically denote by $f^{\ast }$). </p>
